.TH CLINE-CONSOLE 1 "2026-08-11" "cline-console 0.13.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cline-console \- control the Cline extension running in a VS Code workspace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cline-console
.RI [ global-options ]
.I resource action
.RI [ action-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cline-console
is a local control plane for the Cline extension running inside VS Code.
It routes terminal requests through one user service to a companion extension
in the selected workspace. Cline remains the execution engine and continues to
own providers, history, approvals, checkpoints, tools, terminals, and its user
interface.
.PP
Resources are
.BR task ,
.BR queue ,
.BR workspace ,
and
.BR service .
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-workspace " " path
Select an exact registered workspace or a path contained inside one.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit JSON for commands that support machine-readable output.
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable ANSI terminal colors.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
Set the timeout used by interactive collision prompts. The value must be
positive. The default is 30 seconds.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command help and exit.
.SH TASK COMMANDS
.TP
.B task start --file FILE
Start one task using the exact UTF-8 contents of
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B task start --text TEXT
Start one task from inline text.
.TP
.B task start --stdin
Read one task from standard input.
.TP
.B task send --file FILE
Send a follow-up using the exact contents of
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B task send --text TEXT
Send an inline follow-up. A follow-up for a running task is persisted in the
workspace FIFO; otherwise it is delivered immediately.
.TP
.B task status
Display the latest reconciled task for one selected workspace, including its
state, meaningful title, and matching queued source path when known.
.TP
.B tasks
Display reconciled task state for all registered workspaces, or one workspace
when
.B --workspace
is supplied.
.TP
.B task stop
Stop the selected task through Cline's normal cancellation path. An explicit
workspace is recommended and required when selection would be ambiguous.
.TP
.B task restart
Restart the latest exact-workspace task using its original full prompt from
Cline history.
.TP
.B tasks finish
Queue every exact-workspace Cline history item ending in
.B resume_task
for completion, oldest first. Already retained queue-history entries are
deduplicated. Cline Legacy does not expose native historical resume, so prompts
are re-run through the normal queue.
.TP
.B task capabilities
Display the detected Cline version and supported adapter operations.
.SH QUEUE COMMANDS
.TP
.B queue list
Display running and waiting FIFO entries. Without
.BR --workspace ,
all registered workspaces are shown.
.TP
.B queue add --file FILE...
Append one or more files in supplied order.
.TP
.B queue add --dir DIRECTORY
Append all regular files discovered recursively in deterministic relative-path
order. Symbolic links are ignored.
.TP
.B queue add --dir DIRECTORY --newer-than REFERENCE_FILE
Append only regular files whose modification time is strictly newer than the
reference file. Deterministic relative-path order is retained.
.TP
.B queue add ... --resume
Append the supplied batch and clear a persisted queue pause.
.TP
.B queue replace --file FILE...
Replace all waiting entries with the supplied batch. A genuinely active running
entry is preserved.
.TP
.B queue replace --dir DIRECTORY
Replace waiting entries with the deterministically ordered directory contents.
.TP
.B queue replace --dir DIRECTORY --newer-than REFERENCE_FILE
Replace waiting entries using the same strict modification-time filter.
.TP
.B queue remove --file PATH
Remove one waiting entry by exact stored source path.
.TP
.B queue remove --title TITLE
Remove one waiting entry by exact displayed title. Ambiguous titles are rejected.
.TP
.B queue remove --id ID
Remove one waiting entry by queue ID.
.TP
.B queue pause
Allow the current task to finish, then prevent the next task from dispatching.
The pause is persisted.
.TP
.B queue resume
Clear the persisted pause and resume FIFO processing.
.TP
.B queue clear
Remove all waiting and running queue entries. Cancel an active task only when it
exactly matches this queue, then delete matching task IDs from Cline history and
per-task storage. Tasks from other workspaces and unrelated manual tasks are
preserved.
.PP
Queued tasks must remain terminal for at least 60 seconds before completion is
recorded. If execution resumes, that confirmation timer resets. The next task
then waits 30 seconds after the confirmed completion or failure.
Workspace activity, pause, clear, replacement, and removal state are rechecked
before dispatch. Queued follow-up messages are not delayed.
.SH WORKSPACE COMMANDS
.TP
.B workspace list
List registered VS Code filesystem workspaces and their local endpoints.
.TP
.B workspace clear
Require an explicit workspace, clear its entire queue, cancel its displayed
Cline task, and delete all Cline history and per-task storage owned by that
exact workspace. Other workspaces are preserved.
.SH SERVICE COMMANDS
.TP
.B service install
Install, enable, and start the singleton systemd user service.
.TP
.B service start
Start the user service.
.TP
.B service stop
Stop the user service.
.TP
.B service restart
Restart the user service.
.TP
.B service status
Report whether the service and local socket are available.
.TP
.B service run
Run the singleton routing service in the foreground.
.SH INTERACTIVE BEHAVIOR
Starting a task while another task is active prompts to queue, interrupt and
replace, or abort. Adding files while a task is incomplete and waiting prompts
to restart that task from its original prompt, skip that exact task for queue
processing, or abort. Timeout, EOF, and non-interactive input abort safely.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
Pre-0.12 commands including
.BR new ,
.BR send ,
.BR add ,
.BR resume ,
.BR cancel ,
.BR status ,
.BR "task list" ,
.BR workspaces ,
bare
.BR queue ,
and
.B queue pop
remain operational as deprecated aliases. They print migration guidance and
retain their previous behavior.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable ANSI colors when set.
.TP
.B TERM
The value
.B dumb
disables ANSI colors.
.TP
.B CLINE_DIR
Override the Cline session metadata directory used for compatibility detection.
.TP
.B CLINE_VSCODE_STORAGE_DIR
Override the Cline VS Code global-storage directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cline-console/service.sock
Singleton user-service socket.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cline-console/queue-*.json
Private persisted per-workspace queues.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/cline-console/cline-console.log
Default log file. Prompt and message bodies are not logged.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/cline-console.service
Generated systemd user unit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed, including a safe user-selected or timeout abort.
.TP
.B 1
Validation, routing, compatibility, workspace, or service failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start a task from a file:
.PP
.nf
cline-console -w /repo task start --file task.md
.fi
.PP
Append and resume a batch:
.PP
.nf
cline-console -w /repo queue add --file one.md two.md --resume
.fi
.PP
Inspect every queue:
.PP
.nf
cline-console queue list
.fi
.PP
Remove one waiting item by ID:
.PP
.nf
cline-console -w /repo queue remove --id 01274731-fd91-4f2f-a239-7917799b87ae
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR code (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/bvrznski/cline-console/issues.
